subtitle: Californians say how AI should be built, governed, and used
----

# Keep humans in the loop

We asked Californians some of the hardest questions facing the state:

*How is AI reshaping work and the economy? What should government do about it?*

----
id: public_forum
----

## A public forum on AI

In May 2026, we opened a public forum on the Impact of AI on work. Over many months, a cross-section of the public came together to give us their thoughts. They took polls and joined facilitated group discussions. They shared their own experiences, and listened to their peers. Then they refined gut reactions into concrete policy ideas.

One idea came up consistently: **We need humans in the AI policy loop.** Not only in how AI tools are used day-to-day, but in how they are built and governed.

