----
id: tier_1_idea_1
title: Hold AI companies liable for harm they cause
----

Participants wanted clear accountability when AI systems cause damage, placing responsibility on the companies that build and deploy them rather than on the people affected.

- Make companies accountable and enact criminal liability for any harm their AI products cause
- Increase capacity / resources for effective enforcement

----
id: tier_1_idea_2
title: Protect people and nature from the resource needs of data centers
----

Concern about the physical footprint of AI, its demands on energy, water, and land, and a call to shield communities and the environment from those costs.

- Scrutiny of the impact of data centers/physical systems on environment
- Specific limits set for the amount of water, water discharge, and energy usage, and other potential local impacts (e.g. noise output) by data centers/companies and should be rigorously tested and reviewed

----
id: tier_1_idea_3
title: Set rules for where AI can be used safely
----

Set domain-specific rules that keep human judgment in the decisions that most affect people's lives.

- Regulate how AI is used to make decisions that impact lives
- Automation technologies used in the hiring process should be banned

----
